    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Diaphragm position


    The diaphragm is located at the inferior-most
    aspect of the ribcage, filling the inferior thoracic aperture. It acts as the
    floor of the thoracic cavity and the roof of the abdominal cavity. The attachments
    of diaphragm can be divided into peripheral and central attachments. It has three
    peripheral attachments:



    Lumbar vertebrae and arcuate ligaments.

    Costal
    cartilages of ribs 7-10 (attach directly to ribs 11-12).

    Xiphoid process
    of the sternum.


'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 817113b8cb5de3145817c278285a3e47, type: 2}
