      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Heart Position in Chest\n\nThe heart is located within the rib cage, under
    and slightly to the left of the breastbone (sternum). It approximately the size
    of a clenched fist. The lungs surround the right and left side of the heart.
    \r\n\r\nThe heart and lungs are located in the thorax, or chest cavity. The heart
    pumps blood from the body to the lungs, where the blood is oxygenated. It then
    returns the blood to the heart, which pumps the freshly oxygenated blood to the
    rest of the body."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 817113b8cb5de3145817c278285a3e47, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -4709617436596681206, guid: 817113b8cb5de3145817c278285a3e47, type: 2}
